   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "17 King's Parade (Caffe Nero). Mock-Tudor black-and-white timber front, jettied 1st and 2nd floors on carved brackets, three multi-pane windows per floor in black frames, a pierced/fretted decorative eaves board (cornice 'bracketed') and three small gabled dormers on the tiled roof. Light-blue Caffe Nero awning with navy lettering, navy fascia 'THE ITALIAN COFFEE Co' below, green moulded beam above the shopfront; hanging blue Caffe Nero sign at the north edge."
